    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 260 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `AcceptanceTest` and the 27 existing `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping sequence numbers entirely. Every value derived from the customer code now flows from this new identity.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (the create path):\n- Replaced the old `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` \u2014 which built `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` using a per-city sequence \u2014 with `nextCustomerCode(region, normalizedTelephone, lastName)` producing `region + \"-\" + HASH8`.\n- Added `hash8(...)`: first 8 upper-case hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`.\n- Added `region(postcode, city)` / `regionForPostcode(postcode)`: region is derived from the postcode (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), falling back to the city-to-region table, else `UNKNOWN`.\n- The call site now passes the normalized E.164 telephone, the postcode-derived region, and the last name. Removed the now-unused `prefix3` helper and added the `MessageDigest` import.\n\nBecause the membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), its Luhn check digit (over the digits in the code), and the create audit record all read `customerCode`, they automatically reflect the new region-and-hash identity.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** (`formatLocality`):\n- Locality now derives from the identity \u2014 it reads the `REGION` segment (the part before the first `-`) of the customer code, falling back to direct postcode/city resolution only when no code is present. Updated the membership-number javadoc example.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: Updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` field descriptions/examples to document the new format.\n\nThe audit log confirms the change end-to-end: `owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...`.",
